        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Organizations: AbsolutePunk\n- People: Paramore\n- Products: “Always Summer”, “Decode”, Twilight soundtrack\n- Places: Franklin, Tennessee\n\nFacts:\n- Paramore is an American rock band from Franklin, Tennessee, formed in 2004.\n- “Decode” is a song by Paramore created for the soundtrack of the 2008 romantic fantasy film Twilight.\n- On May 21, 2012 at 8:00 PM EST, the song “Always Summer” premiered on AbsolutePunk.\n- AbsolutePunk mainly focused on artists who were relatively unknown to mainstream audiences.\n- AbsolutePunk was known for featuring artists who later achieved crossover success, including Blink-182, Fall Out Boy, My Chemical Romance, New Found Glory, Brand New, Taking Back Sunday, The Gaslight Anthem, Anberlin, Thrice, All Time Low, Jack's Mannequin, Yellowcard, Paramore, Relient K, and A Day to Remember.",
